#. the name of this language in the language itself — "Deutsch", not
#. "German". A list of languages is read by the people who speak them.
msgid "English"
msgstr "Deutsch"

#. what this module is called, wherever the interface names it
#: module.yaml
msgid "Recovery"
msgstr "Recovery"

#. what it is, in one sentence, under the row that starts the work
#: module.yaml
msgid "Repair an Arch Linux system that is already on a disk."
msgstr "Ein Arch-Linux-System reparieren, das schon auf einem Datenträger liegt."

#. the row that starts the work
#: module.yaml
msgid "Repair"
msgstr "Reparieren"

#. the row that opens every answer, and the heading over that page
#: module.yaml
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr "Konfiguration"

#. ARCH_OS_RECOVERY_KEYMAP: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Console keyboard"
msgstr "Konsolentastatur"

#. ARCH_OS_RECOVERY_KEYMAP: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "The keyboard you are typing on right now. It is loaded immediately, and opens on the layout this live image was started with."
msgstr "Die Tastatur, auf der du tippst. Sie wird hier und jetzt geladen und steht anfangs auf der Belegung, mit der dieses Live-Abbild gestartet wurde."

#. ARCH_OS_RECOVERY_KEYMAP: the heading its row sits under
#: module.yaml
msgid "Region"
msgstr "Region"

#. ARCH_OS_RECOVERY_DISK: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Disk"
msgstr "Datenträger"

#. ARCH_OS_RECOVERY_DISK: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "The disk holding the Arch OS installation to repair. Opening it does not change anything on it."
msgstr "Der Datenträger mit der Arch-OS-Installation, die repariert werden soll. Ihn zu öffnen ändert nichts daran."

#. ARCH_OS_RECOVERY_DISK: the heading its row sits under
#: module.yaml
msgid "Storage"
msgstr "Speicher"

#. ARCH_OS_RECOVERY_DISK: what a wrong answer is told
#: module.yaml
msgid "Choose a disk that exists."
msgstr "Wähle einen vorhandenen Datenträger."

#. ARCH_OS_RECOVERY_ENCRYPTED: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Disk encryption"
msgstr "Verschlüsselung"

#. ARCH_OS_RECOVERY_ENCRYPTED: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "Whether that disk is encrypted with LUKS."
msgstr "Ob dieser Datenträger mit LUKS verschlüsselt ist."

#. ARCH_OS_RECOVERY_PASSWORD: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Encryption password"
msgstr "Verschlüsselungspasswort"

#. ARCH_OS_RECOVERY_PASSWORD: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "The password that unlocks that disk. It is asked for right before the recovery starts and is never written to a file."
msgstr "Das Passwort, das diesen Datenträger entsperrt. Es wird unmittelbar vor dem Start der Wiederherstellung abgefragt und nie in eine Datei geschrieben."

#. ARCH_OS_RECOVERY_PASSWORD: what a wrong answer is told
#: module.yaml
msgid "That password does not unlock this disk."
msgstr "Dieses Passwort entsperrt diesen Datenträger nicht."

#. ARCH_OS_RECOVERY_SNAPSHOT: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Snapshot"
msgstr "Schnappschuss"

#. ARCH_OS_RECOVERY_SNAPSHOT: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "The snapshot to put in place of the root subvolume. Newest first, with the date it was taken and what created it."
msgstr "Der Schnappschuss, der an die Stelle des Wurzel-Subvolumes tritt. Der neueste zuerst, mit dem Zeitpunkt der Aufnahme und dem Anlass."

#. the header's status, while its check says yes
#: ../../oak.yaml
msgid "Online"
msgstr "Online"

#. the header's status, while its check says no
#: ../../oak.yaml
msgid "Offline"
msgstr "Offline"

#. the step, as the run lists it
#: tasks/@repair/open/task.yaml
msgid "Unlock and mount the system"
msgstr "System entsperren und einhängen"

#. the step, as the run lists it
#: tasks/@repair/rollback/task.yaml
msgid "Go back to a snapshot"
msgstr "Auf einen Schnappschuss zurückgehen"

#. asked before the step runs
#: tasks/@repair/rollback/task.yaml
msgid ""
"Put {{ARCH_OS_RECOVERY_SNAPSHOT}} in place of the root subvolume on {{ARCH_OS_RECOVERY_DISK}}?\n"
"\n"
"The system as it is now is deleted and replaced by that snapshot. Everything under /home is untouched, and so are the other snapshots. You can come back and choose a different one."
msgstr ""
"{{ARCH_OS_RECOVERY_SNAPSHOT}} an die Stelle des Wurzel-Subvolumes auf {{ARCH_OS_RECOVERY_DISK}} setzen?\n"
"\n"
"Das System, wie es jetzt ist, wird gelöscht und durch diesen Schnappschuss ersetzt. Alles unter /home bleibt unangetastet, die übrigen Schnappschüsse ebenfalls. Du kannst wiederkommen und einen anderen wählen."

#. the step, as the run lists it
#: tasks/@repair/kernel/task.yaml
msgid "Rebuild the boot files"
msgstr "Startdateien neu bauen"

#. asked before the step runs
#: tasks/@repair/kernel/task.yaml
msgid ""
"Rebuild the kernel images and the initial ram disks?\n"
"\n"
"Needed after a rollback that goes back past a kernel update: the modules in the restored system and the images in /boot would then belong to different kernels, and the machine would come up without a single module. Everything is taken from the package cache, so this needs no network."
msgstr ""
"Die Kernel-Abbilder und die Initial-RAM-Disks neu bauen?\n"
"\n"
"Nötig nach einem Rücksprung über ein Kernel-Update hinweg: Die Module im wiederhergestellten System und die Abbilder in /boot sind dann zwei verschiedene Kernel, und der Rechner startet ohne ein einziges Modul. Alles kommt aus dem Paket-Cache, ein Netzwerk braucht es dafür nicht."

#. an action: its row, and the heading over its page
#: actions/chroot/action.yaml
msgid "Open a shell"
msgstr "Shell öffnen"

#. an action: what it does, under its row
#: actions/chroot/action.yaml
msgid "Inside the system on the disk, to look around or fix something by hand. Leave it with exit."
msgstr "Im System auf dem Datenträger, um dich umzusehen oder etwas von Hand zu reparieren. Verlassen mit exit."

#. an action: its row, and the heading over its page
#: actions/live-image/action.yaml
msgid "An Arch Linux live image"
msgstr "Ein Arch-Linux-Live-Image"

#. an action: what a no from it means
#: actions/live-image/action.yaml
msgid "This runs from a booted Arch Linux live image. Write one with Create boot medium, start the machine from it, and open this there."
msgstr "Das läuft auf einem gestarteten Arch-Linux-Live-Image. Schreib eins mit Bootmedium erstellen, starte die Maschine davon und öffne es dort."

#. an action: its row, and the heading over its page
#: actions/no-cable/action.yaml
msgid "No internet over a cable"
msgstr "Kein Internet über ein Kabel"

#. an action: its row, and the heading over its page
#: actions/restart/action.yaml
msgid "Restart"
msgstr "Neu starten"

#. an action: what it does, under its row
#: actions/restart/action.yaml
msgid "Close this machine down and start it again."
msgstr "Den Rechner herunterfahren und neu starten."

#. an action: its row, and the heading over its page
#: actions/root/action.yaml
msgid "Running as root"
msgstr "Läuft als root"

#. an action: what a no from it means
#: actions/root/action.yaml
msgid "This has to run as root. Log in as root and start it again."
msgstr "Das muss als root laufen. Melde dich als root an und starte es erneut."

#. an action: its row, and the heading over its page
#: actions/share-log/action.yaml
msgid "Share the log"
msgstr "Log teilen"

#. an action: what it does, under its row
#: actions/share-log/action.yaml
msgid "Put the log of this run online at paste.rs for whoever is helping. Anyone with the address can read it; passwords are never in it."
msgstr "Stellt das Log dieses Laufs auf paste.rs online, für die Person, die dir hilft. Jede Person mit der Adresse kann es lesen; Passwörter stehen nie darin."

#. an action: what a no from it means
#: actions/share-log/action.yaml
msgid "The log could not be put online. Is this machine online?"
msgstr "Das Log ließ sich nicht online stellen. Ist diese Maschine online?"

#. read once the action is done, and held on until somebody has
#: actions/share-log/action.yaml
msgid ""
"Log shared\n"
"\n"
"Scan the code, or read the address under it, and hand it to whoever is helping."
msgstr ""
"Log geteilt\n"
"\n"
"Scanne den Code oder lies die Adresse darunter und gib sie an die Person, die dir hilft."

#. an action: its row, and the heading over its page
#: actions/shutdown/action.yaml
msgid "Shut down"
msgstr "Herunterfahren"

#. an action: what it does, under its row
#: actions/shutdown/action.yaml
msgid "Switch this machine off."
msgstr "Den Rechner ausschalten."

#. an action: its row, and the heading over its page
#: actions/wifi/action.yaml actions/wifi-passphrase/action.yaml
msgid "Wireless network"
msgstr "WLAN"

#. an action: what it does, under its row
#: actions/wifi/action.yaml
msgid "Join a wireless network."
msgstr "Mit einem WLAN verbinden."

#. ARCH_OS_WIFI_SSID: the page of the action
#: actions/wifi/action.yaml
msgid "Network"
msgstr "Netzwerk"

#. an action: its row, and the heading over its page
#: actions/wifi-card/action.yaml
msgid "A wireless card"
msgstr "Eine WLAN-Karte"

#. an action: what a no from it means
#: actions/wifi-passphrase/action.yaml
msgid "{{ARCH_OS_WIFI_SSID}} did not accept that passphrase, or it is out of range."
msgstr "{{ARCH_OS_WIFI_SSID}} hat dieses Passwort nicht angenommen oder ist außer Reichweite."

#. ARCH_OS_WIFI_PASSPHRASE: the page of the action
#: actions/wifi-passphrase/action.yaml
msgid "Passphrase"
msgstr "Passwort"
